WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:34.480
Rin Rin Deeply Moved! Panda's House!

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.410
Would these flowers be okay?

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.370
Y-Yes, please! That would be perfect.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.630
Please come again!

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.950
Okay!

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.700
He's so cool!

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:46.970
Yeah!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.250
Panda!

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.220
You must be tired from working! 
Here, have these.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.590
I guess I'll take them.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.180
See ya.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.140
Panda...

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.850
You can be so heartless.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.360
Oh, Panda.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.780
I just want to be friends with you.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.740
"It's okay.
You'll be friends someday."

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.530
You're right!

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.700
Of course!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.680
Pandas are amazing!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.010
Yay!

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.030
Yes, this is Florist Rin Rin.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.350
An arrangement with bamboo 
as the main piece?

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.820
Yes, I can do that.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.090
Where should I deliver it to?

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.300
Rin Rin is so annoying.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.270
Rin Rin?

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.630
The florist?

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:48.670
Yep.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.940
Every time I pass by...

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:52.940
Here, have this.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:54.440
You like this, right?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.650
Pandas are so cute!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.540
Seems like a nice guy.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.070
Really?

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:07.370
But the panda items he 
gives me are so tacky.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.570
Like this.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.290
Oh, that's cute!

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.240
Really? You think so?

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.700
Then why don't you give 
it to Miss Sasako?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.040
I'm not giving it away.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.840
See, you do like it.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.560
Rin Rin's so annoying.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.910
What if he was at your house right now?

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.150
Don't say things like that.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.440
Panda

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.930
This is Panda's house.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.990
I'm here to deliver flowers.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.000
I wonder where Panda is...

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.920
He's probably at 
Polar Bear's Café at this hour.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.880
Hello, thank you for your hard work.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.800
Is something the matter?

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.300
<i>It's a panda! Panda Mama!</i>

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.720
Oh, excuse me.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.760
Y-Yes.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.310
I'll pay this separately,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.060
but would you mind rearranging 
the bamboo in the rooms, too?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.610
You mean I can come 
into your house?!

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.200
It seems that Rin Rin has
 an intense love of pandas.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.060
Apparently his collection of

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.120
panda merchandise is quite extensive.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.340
He should have opened up

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.420
a panda merchandise shop 
instead of a flower shop.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.480
He has his reasons.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.120
Like what?

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:40.070
When the young Rin Rin 
was traveling the world

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.240
to collect panda merchandise,

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.760
he was involved in an incident...

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.140
You're lying, aren't you?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:49.910
Yes.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.420
Why do you lie?

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.560
I want to bring some color

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.400
into your desolate lives with a modest lie.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.090
Well, excuse me for having a desolate life!

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.030
Let's stop talking about Rin Rin.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:04.900
There.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.970
How's that?

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.760
Oh, that's wonderful.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.780
Here, I'll pay you right now.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.320
Just one moment.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.790
<i>This is where Panda lives.</i>

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.170
He's so cute.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.170
Hello.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.770
Mama asked me to bring you some tea.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.430
<i>It's a panda! Little Sister Panda!</i>

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.370
I'll set it right here.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:42.180
Thank you, um...

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.990
Please call me Mei Mei.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.990
You're Rin Rin, right?

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.480
You know about me?

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.400
You're famous around town 
as the good-looking florist.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.480
So it seems.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.950
You're not very humble, are you?

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:00.600
But you know, you're not my type.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.090
You're too skinny.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.820
Oh well, I'll play with 
you for a little while.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.250
Let's play tag.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.750
Oh, sorry, I actually need
 to get back to my shop...

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.520
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mr. Rin Rin.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.000
Oh?

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.940
Wait!

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:28.800
<i>I'm chasing a panda!</i>

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.370
<i>I'm spinning with a panda!</i>

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:39.240
<i>I'm rolling around with a panda!</i>

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.250
<i>What an amazingly happy time!</i>

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.180
Next we're going to play hide and seek.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.140
Playing hide and seek with a panda!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.100
One... two...

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.060
Mr. Rin Rin is quite tough.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.060
three... four... five...

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.690
Hey, where are you?

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.760
Hey!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:09.640
I wonder if it's okay to keep playing 
and not go back to work.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:15.200
It is!

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.670
Because I'm with pandas!

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.500
I found you!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.460
Who are you?

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.670
What's wrong?

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.660
Oh, Grandpa, what are you doing?

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.980
Grandpa?

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.390
You intruder!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.430
No, Rin Rin is a florist.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:45.110
Every day is a good day.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.130
Consider the whole.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:49.450
High pressure west, low pressure east.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.530
You always play dumb 
when things go wrong.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.530
A good and wise mother.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.320
Curbside parking.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.250
It's a panda.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:01.820
Panda Grandpa's... tai-chi!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.340
So, it wasn't a panda 
merchandise store...

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.300
but a flower shop that he started.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.850
It's so sad.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:16.290
I know it's made up, 
but I still can't stop crying.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:21.080
I may feel like being nice to Rin Rin.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.950
He has his reasons.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:27.420
It was there in that glaring, 
cruel land...

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:30.310
No, that's enough already.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:38.740
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.250
Huh?

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:45.360
Where am I?

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.770
Ow.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.360
Oh, that's right.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:52.020
I came to deliver flowers 
to Panda's house and...

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.460
This isn't good.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:56.410
I have to hurry and get 
back to the shop.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:01.010
T-This is, Panda's...

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.520
Could this room be...

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.130
Panda's room?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.390
Panda's bed!

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.320
Panda's panda cushion!

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.190
Panda's panda slippers!

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.880
Panda's sticker!

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.260
This is the present I gave him.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.620
He <i>is</i> taking good care of it.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.870
Baby pandas!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.220
They're so cute!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.480
I want to touch them.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.530
No, no, that's for decoration.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:56.740
You're giving it to me?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.370
So cute!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.850
Are you awake?

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:06.860
Sorry about that. Grandpa's a little...

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:07.410
Oh?

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:10.350
Thank you. It tastes really good.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.730
Rin Rin, that's for decoration...

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.130
Or rather, do you eat bamboo grass?

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.590
Yes, in certain situations.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.760
Well, I won't stop you...

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.970
Um, I haven't paid you 
for the flowers yet.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.490
I don't need payment.

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:30.100
May I just hold the baby pandas?

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.990
Sure, but I'll still pay you.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.450
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.580
My children are rather shy.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:47.840
I'm in heaven!

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:00.720
Would these flowers be okay?

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.640
I wonder what happened to Mr. Rintaro?

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.180
He was all scratched up.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:15.150
A book on understanding 
animal feelings

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.410
I was able to become 
friends with Panda's mom

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.160
and little sister.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.620
Next is Panda's grandpa and the babies.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.770
And someday...

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.880
Hey, Mr. Handa.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.760
On our way home today...

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:24.930
Not today. I have plans today.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.310
Just for a little while?

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.830
You don't have a girlfriend, 
so you should be free.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:35.930
Jeez, I wish girls would follow me
 instead of you, Panda.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.300
Hey, that's mean.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.550
<i>"Instead of pandas?"</i>

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.830
<i>I'm jealous!</i>

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.890
I feel like someone's staring at me.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.270
Really?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:12:00.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:05.910
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:05.240
Mr. Penguin's Confession!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.540
The croissant is good, too.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:15.580
I think it would taste even better 
if they added bamboo leaves.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.380
I'm not sure about that.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.510
More importantly, I hear they 
have a panda red bean bun, too.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.980
Really?

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:23.340
Hey, Mr. Penguin.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.410
Next time, could you get the 
panda red bean bun, too?

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.850
What the heck?!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:30.830
I'm not going to the 
bakery to buy pastries!

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.400
I want to...

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.570
ask Miss Penko out on a date.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.230
I know that.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.980
But every time you go,

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.440
you just come back 
with lots of bread.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.620
Well...

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.900
Why not just ask her out 
and be done with it?

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.570
B-But...

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:51.410
When you fear taking the small step,

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.040
it is time to take the big step.

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:57.870
It's an old French aphorism.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.060
Taking the big step...

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.090
I'm lying.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:05.590
The small step...

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.970
The big step...

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:09.530
I've made up my mind!

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:10.730
I'm going to do it!

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.250
You're going to do it? You mean...

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.060
I'm going to confess my love to Miss Penko.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.350
Confess <i>(kokuhaku)</i>?

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.890
Sorry! I don't have time 
for your puns right now!

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.280
I'm going right now!

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:30.330
There he goes.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.430
Haha!

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:36.270
That's... heinous <i>(gokuaku)</i>?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.010
Yes.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:44.170
But how should I do it?

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.180
You didn't plan it out?

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.710
Of course not!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.800
I just thought of doing 
this a second ago.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.990
What should I do?

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.670
Well, for example, a peacock 
spreads its feathers

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.520
as a show of affection.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:02.550
I see.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.490
Like this?

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.020
That's rather dull.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.240
What else, then?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.460
A frigatebird inflates his red gular pouch.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.730
There doesn't seem to be 
much of a difference.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.200
Can't you make it bigger?

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:33.690
Tortoises attack the shell, 
bite, and then mount.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.560
Really? Like pro wrestling?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.430
Wouldn't biting be against the rules?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.920
How under-handed. That's so cool!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:44.390
Wait, Mr. Penguin 
doesn't have a shell.

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.900
He could wear a plate.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.980
A kappa?

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:54.100
What do kappas do when they confess?

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:58.630
Hey! Help me think 
about this seriously!

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:02.380
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.600
This is awful. 
It's the end of the world.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:10.100
I think something simple like 
"I like you," is best.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.930
Isn't that a bit overt?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:16.460
But then she'll know that I like her.

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.540
I thought that was the idea.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.940
T-That's right.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.900
Okay. I'll do my best 
with the simplest way.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.930
Well then, let's go.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:28.780
You're going, too?!

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:32.080
An old general once said:

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:35.830
"A single arrow may break, 
but three will not."

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.440
Well then,

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.360
Three heads are better than one 
<i>(sannin yoreba monju no chie)</i>.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.120
A monkey's wisdom <i>(monkey no chie)</i>?

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.330
That would make it shallow 
cleverness <i>(sarujie)</i>.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:56.420
I'll be fine on my own, so stay here!

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.880
I hope everything goes well.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:01.710
Huh?

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.690
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.480
I-I like you.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.020
Please, take these.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:15.620
A-All right, I can do this. 
I can do this!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.060
Here I go. Yes, here I go!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.350
I-I like you.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.930
Please, take these.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.390
Got it.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.810
I-I like you, Miss Penko!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.770
Please, take these.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.230
I-I like you.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:52.740
I like you. Please, take these!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.280
I like you. Please, take these!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.520
What's he doing?

00:16:54.830 --> 00:17:11.530
I like you. Please, take these!

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.200
Is that some kind of magic spell?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.350
Those who are in love

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:04.590
will repeat actions over and over,
 even knowing they are senseless.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.040
Another old aphorism?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:11.200
No, it's an aphorism that
 Mr. Penguin will create in the future.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:12.760
I like you!

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:21.540
Maybe it's impossible 
for me to confess.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:34.610
<i>If she were to accept my love...</i>

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:38.450
I'm very happy, Miss Penko.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.640
I'm very happy, Miss Penko.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.240
This is delicious, Miss Penko.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.380
I'm very happy!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.790
Oh, no.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:54.630
That's not good, 
I got lost in my dream world.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.280
But there's a possibility that 
my dream will become a reality.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.420
I have to keep trying for that reason!

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.440
Thank goodness, he's finally going.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.420
Yes, good.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.940
<i>I'm going to do it.</i>

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.400
<i>I will!</i>

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.320
Miss Penko—

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:40.460
Mr. Penguin's still out cold.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.900
Maybe I'll go home.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:52.470
Huh? I was...

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.570
That's right! I was going 
to confess to Miss Penko!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.650
But maybe not today.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:02.370
I feel like I'm going in circles.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.540
No! There's no time like the present!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.020
But then again...

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:10.330
I don't think I'm at my best today.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.620
No! I can't keep being so negative!

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.300
But then again...

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:18.300
Are you done yet?

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.990
We're getting tired of waiting.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.390
What are you two doing here?!

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.260
I told you not to come!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:28.640
Hurry up. I'm hungry.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.550
Not my problem!

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.440
Are you not going to confess?

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.980
W-Well...

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.900
An old Roman poet said this:

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.410
"Love and good luck 
lies with the hero."

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.740
With the hero?

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:51.660
So good luck and love are at 
this hero person's place?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.950
Let's go there now.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.180
I'm <i>going</i> to Miss Penko.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:56.380
Really?

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.320
All right, here I go.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:03.030
Er, both of you, don't follow me!

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.040
<i>I'm going to say it. 
I'm going to say it!</i>

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.750
Why do you always butt in at times like these?!

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:22.040
I heard about their 
panda-shaped red bean buns.

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.960
All right! I'll buy you one!

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:26.500
So, go home! Go home, go home!

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:31.280
Um...

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.730
Um...

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.820
I wonder if he's okay.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.670
Hey!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.610
I did it! I did it!

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.750
Congratulations, Mr. Penguin!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:07.070
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.540
So, it went well?

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:13.240
I don't know what to say.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.930
So what did Miss Penko say?

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.020
You want to know?

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.260
Come on, give us the details.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:23.430
Well, you see,

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:27.220
Miss Penko apparently remembered me.

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:32.180
She said I could have these!

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:35.170
Ten of these tickets can be exchanged
 for 500 yen worth of either bread, jam, or butter.
Expires three months after issue date.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.140
She gave me these service tickets!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.230
She said I could have extra, 
so she gave me three!

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:48.900
She gave me extra service tickets!

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:52.040
Um... what happened to confessing?

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.050
That's not important right now!

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:57.170
I sort of touched her hand 
when she gave me these!

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.420
What should I do? 
I'm not washing my hand!

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:02.480
I'm not washing my hands! 
I don't want to wash my hands!

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.380
Um...

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:08.610
One service ticket is a service ticket, 
but three service tickets...

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:10.560
I don't want to use them! 
Don't want to use them!

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:11.110
...are just service tickets.

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:13.150
You shouldn't say that.

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:15.580
Are you listening, Panda?

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:16.830
I'm listening.

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:18.310
Look, Miss Sasako!

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:22.310
I'm so happy!

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:25.470
Next Time

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:59.360
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:01.810
You usually only say my 
name twice, what's wrong?

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:03.330
Nothing is wrong.

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:08.260
I just wanted a little excitement 
in my boring times with you.

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:09.880
You don't hold back, do you?

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:13.760
Let's figure out why I'm so 
bored when I'm with you.

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.510
Let's not. Polar Bear, finish this.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.640
Next time, Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:20.890
...will be presented in 30 seconds.

00:24:20.890 --> 00:24:22.140
How about 30 minutes?

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:24.950
Mr. Handa's Group Blind Date?
Mr. Handa's Group Blind Date!

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:23.470
Enjoy!
